Hello R-SIG-GENETICS members

A reminder - Genetic data can support causal questions when study design receives equal attention. Modern Causal Inference Methods is a 2-day seminar livestreaming October 15?16 with Michael Zyphur (Instats | instats.org). Specify causal estimands, use directed acyclic graphs to examine confounding, and assess identification assumptions in R. Apply matching, weighting, doubly robust estimation, and causal machine learning to genetic and genomic observational studies where treatment effects may differ across groups. Diagnose overlap and balance, then report causal findings with clear limits on interpretation.

Details and registration: https://instats.org/seminar/modern-causal-inference-methods
Further information is available on the seminar page.


Best wishes

Michael Zyphur
Director and Co-founder
